<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vanchi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vanchi was the capital of the early Chera kings according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangam-literature">Sangam literature</a>. Its location is debated: most historians identify it with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karur">Karur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, while others place it near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kodungallur">Kodungallur</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a> coast. The epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silappatikaram">Silappatikaram</a> describes it as the seat of the Chera king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senguttuvan">Senguttuvan</a>.</p></div>
